 "en": "<p>To <b>agree</b> or say the same is true for you, use <b>So / Neither + auxiliary + subject</b>.</p><p>Positive sentence → <b>So</b>: <i>I like tea. — <b>So do I</b>. I'm tired. — <b>So am I</b>. I've finished. — <b>So have I</b>.</i></p><p>Negative sentence → <b>Neither</b> (or Nor): <i>I don't like meetings. — <b>Neither do I</b>. I can't swim. — <b>Neither can I</b>.</i></p><p>Use the <b>same auxiliary</b> as in the first sentence (do/does/did, am/is/are, was/were, have/has, can, will). If the first sentence has no auxiliary, use <b>do / does / did</b>.</p>",
 "ru": "Согласие «я тоже»: So + вспомогательный глагол + подлежащее (So do I, So am I, So have I). «Я тоже нет»: Neither + вспомогательный + подлежащее (Neither do I, Neither can I). Вспомогательный глагол — как в первой фразе; если его нет — do / does / did.",
 "boss": {
  "situation": "Write a short dialogue with a colleague agreeing about work. Use So do I / So am I / Neither do I / Neither can I / So did I.",
  "samples": [
   "A: I'm tired today. B: So am I.",
   "A: I don't like long meetings. B: Neither do I.",
   "A: I sent my report yesterday. B: So did I.",
   "A: I can't open the file. B: Neither can I.",
   "A: I've finished the training. B: So have I."
  ]
 },
